<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE-OMNIA HOLDINGS HALF-YEAR EPS SOARS.</title>
<headline>TABLE-OMNIA HOLDINGS HALF-YEAR EPS SOARS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - eps		    27.8	   vs 0.9</p>
<p>    Net income	     11.0	   vs 0.8</p>
<p>    Share of associates   nil	   vs 1.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  14.1	   vs 0.6 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.2	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Turnover		404.8	   vs 358.5</p>
<p>Full name: Omnia Holdings Limited.</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that in line with past practise, the interim dividend would be considered at the November board meeting.</p>
<p>The strong results were attributed to good growth in its explosives and chemicals divisions, lower financial costs and benefits arising from the sales of the seed division.</p>
<p>Omnia said it anticipated further real growth in earnings for 1997 accompanied by substantial improvement in its debt to equity ratio.</p>
